# CODEOWNERS — ACTIVE since 2026-09-16 (was an all-commented PLACEHOLDER scaffold).
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND, IMPORTANTLY, WHAT IT DOES NOT. CODEOWNERS by itself only AUTO-REQUESTS a
# reviewer when a PR touches a matching path. It does not block anything. Requiring the review is a
# separate branch-protection setting, `require_code_owner_reviews`, and it is deliberately OFF here:
# `main` requires no approving reviews, and `~/.claude/git-hooks/land-pr` enables GitHub auto-merge,
# so turning it on would wedge every solo PR waiting for an approval that never comes. Auto-request
# = a nudge; required review = a gate. We want the nudge. If you ever do want the gate, read
# land-pr first and expect to change how work lands.
#
# Syntax: <path-glob>  @org/team  @user
#
# ★ NO `*` LINE, ON PURPOSE. A catch-all owner requests the whole team on every PR, including
# single-skill changes that have a named owner two lines below — the notifications then mean nothing
# and people mute them, which is strictly worse than no CODEOWNERS at all. Only the areas whose
# blast radius genuinely exceeds one skill are listed. Uncovered paths (a single `skills/<skill>/`)
# are the normal case, not an oversight.
#
# ★ LAST MATCH WINS, not most-specific. GitHub applies the FINAL matching line, so ordering here is
# load-bearing: broad areas first, narrower carve-outs after. Append new rules below, and if you add
# a broad pattern put it ABOVE the narrow ones it would otherwise swallow.
#
# The team is @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology (permission: maintain). A collaborator
# must be a MEMBER of it to be auto-requested — adding a handle to this file is not enough, and a
# non-member owner silently matches nothing.

# Shared engine — every skill imports it; a resolver or dispatcher change fans out into golden
# snapshots across all 22 skill dirs.
/skills/_skills_common/             @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology

# The orchestrator that composes every gate's verdict into a target profile.
/skills/target-profile/             @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology

# Cross-skill conformance guards. These are the tests that stop one skill diverging from the
# framework's contracts, so they should not be relaxed by the PR they are inconveniencing.
/skills/tests/                      @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology

# CI, required checks, and this file.
/.github/                           @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology

# The framework's contract surface: what "done" means, what a skill must emit, and how to become
# a skill author.
/docs/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md         @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology
/docs/UNIFIED_OUTPUT_CONTRACT.md    @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology
/docs/AUTHORING_A_SKILL.md          @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology

# Trunk-wide instructions and the plugin manifests (a bad edit here misroutes every session or
# breaks every install).
/CLAUDE.md                          @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology
/DEVELOPMENT_GUIDELINES.md          @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology
/.claude-plugin/                    @oneTakeda/rnd-computational-biology-oncology
